     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Substitution w a longer-acting oral stimulant (eg, methylphenidate or amphetamine salts) seems promising, but a 2016 Cochrane review found effectiveness ⍉clearly shown."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "⍉med = approved for methamphetamine use dx; in a phase 3 RCT, mirtazapine 30 mg daily for 12 wks cut use by 2.2 more days of 28 than placebo, w ⍉sig effect on 2/2 end points (incl methamphetamine-negative oral fluid samples)."
     }
    ]
   }
